{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771201494861,"sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","part":{"id":"prt_c63d48d21001jriI7PUTQmWjxS","sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","messageID":"msg_c63d46375001htKZjz90xu8VKt","type":"tool","callID":"call_6368f7878d594818bda9f38f","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore specs directory","prompt":"Exhaustively explore the specs directory at /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/. Read all specification files to understand the application requirements. Focus on identifying what functionality is specified but not yet implemented. Return a comprehensive summary of all specifications and what's already implemented vs what's missing.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39c2b72d5fferr3GDAlJFz07m0 (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n## Comprehensive Specification Analysis: Game of Life Application\n\nI have exhaustively explored the specs directory and analyzed the implementation. Here is a comprehensive summary of all 12 specification files, their requirements, and the implementation status.\n\n---\n\n## SPECIFICATION FILES OVERVIEW\n\n### 1. **Auto-Advance Transitions** (`auto-advance-transitions.md`)\n**Purpose**: Cinematic level progression with fade transitions\n\n**Key Requirements**:\n- Transition sequence: FINISHED → Fade Out (2s) → Interstitial (2s) → Fade In (2s) → READY\n- Skip mechanism (Space/ESC) at any phase\n- State machine: PLAYING, FADING_OUT, INTERSTITIAL, FADING_IN, READY\n- Black overlay with CSS transitions\n- Interstitial display with level info\n- Audio feedback for transitions\n- Edge case handling: tab visibility, rapid success, last level, interruptions\n- Browser tab pause during transitions\n\n**Implementation Status**: ✅ **FULLY IMPLEMENTED**\n- `useTransition` hook provides complete transition logic\n- `TransitionOverlay` component renders states\n- Skip functionality via Space/ESC working\n- Tab visibility handling implemented\n- Transition sounds integrated\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Expert Settings / Dev Panel** (`expert-settings.md`)\n**Purpose**: Hidden configuration interface for tuning game mechanics\n\n**Key Requirements**:\n- Access via backtick key, Settings → Advanced menu path, or triple-tap (mobile)\n- Configurable parameters:\n  - Movement Detection: centroid history (3-10), movement threshold (0.1-2.0), min cluster size (1-5)\n  - Scoring: mover points/gen (1-100), oscillator points/gen (0-20), score multiplier (0.1-5.0)\n  - Level Generation: base time (10-120s), time increment (0-60s), base flux (5-50), difficulty modes\n  - Grid Sizing: mobile cell size (14-24px), desktop cell size (16-28px), min visible cells\n- Settings persistence in localStorage (`gol-expert-settings`)\n- \"Reset to Defaults\" with confirmation\n- Export/Import settings as JSON\n- Real-time updates, visual indicators for non-default values\n- \"Danger Zone\" for extreme values with warnings\n\n**Implementation Status**: ⚠️ **PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED**\n- ✅ Settings panel exists with all configurable parameters\n- ✅ localStorage persistence working\n- ✅ \"Reset to Defaults\" implemented\n- ✅ Real-time updates working\n- ✅ Validation implemented in `settings.ts`\n- ❌ Backtick key access NOT implemented\n- ❌ Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode menu path NOT implemented\n- ❌ Triple-tap gesture for mobile NOT implemented\n- ❌ Export/Import JSON functionality NOT implemented\n- ❌ Visual indicators for non-default values NOT implemented\n- ❌ Danger Zone section NOT implemented\n- ❌ Tooltip documentation for each parameter NOT implemented\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Level Progression** (`level-progression.md`)\n**Purpose**: Progressive difficulty system with time limits and Flux budget\n\n**Key Requirements**:\n- Level config with level number, time limit, initial Flux\n- 4 difficulty scaling modes: TIME_ONLY, RESOURCE_ONLY, MIXED, EXTREME\n- Default: time increases (45, 60, 75, 90s), constant Flux (20)\n- Level completion when timer reaches 0 OR all cells die\n- Score accumulates across levels (totalScore)\n- No win/lose condition (always advances)\n- Fade transitions between levels\n- Victory screen after final level (default 10 levels)\n- Optional localStorage progress persistence\n\n**Implementation Status**: ✅ **FULLY IMPLEMENTED**\n- `level.ts` provides complete level progression logic\n- All 4 difficulty modes implemented\n- Level generation with configurable parameters\n- High score saving per level\n- Victory screen with total score display\n- Play Again functionality\n- Auto-advance with transitions working\n\n---\n\n### 4. **User Interaction** (`user-interaction.md`)\n**Purpose**: Mouse and touch input for drawing/erasing cells with real-time feedback\n\n**Key Requirements**:\n- Draw mode: place live cells (age=1)\n- Erase mode: remove cells (set to 0)\n- Mouse Down/Move/Up handling\n- Touch Start/Move/End/Cancel with preventDefault\n- Coordinate mapping from canvas to grid\n- Sound generation for interactions\n- Crosshair cursor style\n- Touch action: none on canvas\n- Multi-touch: only first touch used\n\n**Implementation Status**: ✅ **FULLY IMPLEMENTED**\n- `interaction.ts` handles all mouse and touch events\n- `GridInteraction.tsx` component renders grid and handles input\n- Draw/erase modes fully functional\n- Sound integration complete\n- Touch handling with preventDefault\n- Coordinate mapping working\n- Crosshair cursor via CSS\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Grid Interaction** (`grid-interaction.md`)\n**Purpose**: Direct cell placement/removal interface during PLANNING phase\n\n**Key Requirements**:\n- Click to place/remove cells during PLANNING phase\n- START button disabled until ≥1 cell placed\n- Cursor states: default, crosshair (placeable), forbidden (no Flux), minus (removable)\n- Visual feedback: cell preview, fade-in (0.1s), shrink animation (0.15s), red flash (invalid)\n- Mobile: pinch-to-zoom disabled, ripple effect on touch\n- Minimum 44x44px touch targets\n- Disabled during RUNNING/FINISHED phases\n- Canvas rendering recommended for performance\n\n**Implementation Status**: ✅ **FULLY IMPLEMENTED**\n- Cell placement/removal fully functional\n- START button properly disabled\n- Canvas rendering used for performance\n- Phase-based constraints working\n- Flux validation with error feedback\n- Visual animations (fade-in, shrink) implemented\n- Invalid action red flash implemented\n- Mobile touch considerations handled\n\n---\n\n### 6. **UI/Overlay System** (`ui-overlay.md`)\n**Purpose**: Controls, configuration panels, and visual overlays\n\n**Key Requirements**:\n- **Cinematic Intro**: Shows on load, \"CONWAY'S GAME OF LIFE\" with glitch, \"ENTER VOID\" button, 1.2s exit animation\n- **Glass HUD**: Semi-transparent, floating overlay at bottom\n  - Main controls: PLAY/PAUSE, STEP, RANDOM (15% density), CLEAR (red text)\n  - Interaction modes: DRAW, ERASE with active state highlighting\n  - Status controls: Waveform dropdown, Volume slider (0-0.5), Generation counter, Settings toggle (⚙️)\n- **Phase Status Display**: Always visible, shows phase, timer, Flux counter\n- **Settings Panel**:\n  - Speed slider (10-500ms)\n  - Grid size buttons: Small (20×30), Medium (40×50), Large (60×80)\n  - Visuals: Show grid lines checkbox\n  - Audio: Enable sonification checkbox\n  - Expert Settings access\n  - Close button (×)\n- **UI Toggle**: Corner button to show/hide all UI\n- Glass effect: blur, semi-transparent background, border\n- Responsive: Desktop full-width, Mobile stacking/scrolling\n- Minimum 44px touch targets\n\n**Implementation Status**: ✅ **FULLY IMPLEMENTED**\n- `IntroOverlay.tsx` with glitch effect and 1.2s exit\n- `GlassHUD.tsx` with all main controls\n- `SettingsPanel.tsx` with all configuration options\n- `UIToggleButton.tsx` for UI visibility\n- Phase status display working\n- Glass effect CSS implemented\n- Responsive design working\n- All buttons properly disabled based on state\n- Touch targets meet minimum size\n\n---\n\n### 7. **Phase Management** (`phase-management.md`)\n**Purpose**: State machine governing PLANNING → RUNNING → FINISHED phases\n\n**Key Requirements**:\n- **PLANNING**: Unlimited duration, place/remove cells, START button (enabled when ≥1 cell), exit on START click\n- **COUNTDOWN**: 3-2-1 countdown, no input, transition to RUNNING\n- **RUNNING**: Fixed timer (level-specific), cell placement add-only, simulation runs, exit on timer=0 or all cells die\n- **FINISHED**: 2s pause, show score/alive cells, auto-advance after 2s, no carryover to next level\n- State machine with guarded transitions\n- Timer uses Date.now() or performance.now()\n- Simulation stops until countdown completes\n- Level transition: no simulation carryover\n\n**Implementation Status**: ✅ **FULLY IMPLEMENTED**\n- `phase.ts` provides complete state machine\n- `usePhaseTimer` hook manages countdown and timer\n- All three phases fully functional\n- Countdown working (3-2-1)\n- Timer accurately counting down\n- Phase transitions properly guarded\n- \"All cells die\" detection working\n- Fresh start on level transition\n\n---\n\n### 8. **Scoring System** (`scoring-system.md`)\n**Purpose**: Real-time score calculation based on pattern classifications\n\n**Key Requirements**:\n- Per-generation calculation based on cluster classification:\n  - MOVER: 10 points/gen (default)\n  - OSCILLATOR: 2 points/gen (default)\n  - STATIC: 0 points\n- Score multiplier (1.0 default)\n- Real-time score updates every generation\n- Smooth counting animation (lerp 0.2s)\n- Milestone flash every 100 points (optional)\n- Score cap at MAX_SAFE_INTEGER\n- Display: Large number with \"PTS\" label, pulse/flash on gain\n- Optional pattern breakdown: Active Movers, Active Oscillators, Current Rate\n- End-of-level stats: Final score, Time survived, Patterns created\n- Per-level reset (no carryover), high score tracking in localStorage\n\n**Implementation Status**: ✅ **FULLY IMPLEMENTED**\n- `scoring.ts` with complete calculation logic\n- Per-generation scoring functional\n- Score multiplier working\n- MAX_SAFE_INTEGER cap implemented\n- High score persistence in localStorage\n- Score display with pattern breakdown\n- Rate calculation implemented\n- End-of-level stats shown\n- Smooth score display animation\n\n---\n\n### 9. **Movement Detection** (`movement-detection.md`)\n**Purpose**: Detect and classify movement patterns via centroid tracking\n\n**Key Requirements**:\n- Connected component detection (8-connectivity)\n- Centroid tracking across generations (history length default: 5)\n- Classification algorithm:\n  - MOVER: centroid translating (threshold: 0.5 cells)\n  - OSCILLATOR: centroid static but cells changing\n  - STATIC: centroid and cells unchanged\n- Cluster persistence: match by nearest centroid, handle splits/merges\n- Minimum cluster size (default: 1)\n- Performance: process <16ms for 60fps\n- Performance indicators: \"active patterns\" count, highlight moving patterns\n- Edge cases: cluster splits/merges, oscillator periods, glider guns\n\n**Implementation Status**: ✅ **FULLY IMPLEMENTED**\n- `movement.ts` with complete tracking logic\n- Connected component detection functional\n- Centroid tracking with history\n- Classification algorithm working\n- Cluster matching by nearest centroid\n- Performance optimized\n- Active patterns count in HUD\n- Movers/Oscillators breakdown in display\n- Minimum cluster size filter implemented\n\n---\n\n### 10. **Canvas Rendering** (`canvas-rendering.md`)\n**Purpose**: High-performance rendering with age-based neon colors and glow\n\n**Key Requirements**:\n- Dark neon theme: background #0a0a0f, grid lines #1a1a2e\n- Age-based colors:\n  - Age 0: #00ffff (cyan), blur 15px\n  - Age 1-2: #61dafb (React blue), blur 8px\n  - Age 3-5: #ff00ff (magenta), blur 4px\n  - Age 6+: #4a00ff (deep purple), blur 2px\n- Cell size: responsive (18px mobile, 20px desktop)\n- Square cells with 2px corner radius\n- Grid lines toggle (G key), only when not running\n- DPR scaling for sharp rendering\n- Intensity metric: active cells / 500 (0-1 range)\n- Minimize context state changes\n- Touch coordinates mapped to canvas space\n\n**Implementation Status**: ✅ **FULLY IMPLEMENTED**\n- `canvasUtils.ts` provides rendering utilities\n- `CanvasGrid.tsx` component renders efficiently\n- All age-based colors and blur effects implemented\n- Responsive cell sizing working\n- Grid lines toggle functional\n- DPR scaling implemented\n- Intensity CSS variable set\n- Performance optimized with minimal state changes\n- Touch coordinate mapping working\n\n---\n\n### 11. **Audio Sonification** (`audio-sonification.md`)\n**Purpose**: Real-time sounds based on births and interactions\n\n**Key Requirements**:\n- SoundEngine class with methods:\n  - setEnabled, setVolume, setWaveform\n  - playGenerationSound(bornCount, avgRow, totalRows)\n  - playInteractionSound('draw' | 'erase')\n- Generation sounds: pitch based on average row (higher rows = higher pitch), intensity based on birth count\n- Interaction sounds: draw (880Hz, high pitch), erase (440Hz, low pitch)\n- Waveforms: sine (default), triangle, square, sawtooth\n- Volume: 0-0.5, default 0.1, 0.01 step\n- Lazy initialization on first sound (browser autoplay policy)\n- Quick attack, exponential decay envelope\n- Concurrent sounds allowed (polyphonic)\n\n**Implementation Status**: ✅ **FULLY IMPLEMENTED**\n- `SoundEngine` class with all methods\n- Generation sounds with pitch mapping\n- Interaction sounds implemented\n- All waveforms supported\n- Volume control working\n- Lazy initialization implemented\n- Proper envelope shaping\n- Additional sounds added: level complete, level start, transition, simulation start, flux error\n- Context resume on user interaction\n\n---\n\n### 12. **Flux Management** (`flux-management.md`)\n**Purpose**: Resource management for strategic cell placement\n\n**Key Requirements**:\n- Initial allocation: 20 Flux per level (configurable 5-50)\n- Placement cost: 1 Flux per cell (both phases)\n- Refund: 1 Flux on cell removal during PLANNING phase only\n- No refunds during RUNNING phase (add-only only)\n- Zero state: placement disabled with visual/audio feedback\n- State: current, initial, placed, removed\n- Validation: Cannot place if Flux < 1, refund only PLANNING, no remove RUNNING\n- HUD display: bottom center, bar or counter, color coding (green/yellow/orange/red)\n- Feedback: Error sound/red flash (insufficient), plop sound/fade-in (placement), suction/shrink (removal)\n- Resets every level (no carryover)\n\n**Implementation Status**: ✅ **FULLY IMPLEMENTED**\n- `flux.ts` provides complete Flux management\n- Placement and removal logic functional\n- Phase-based refund constraints working\n- Zero state with proper feedback implemented\n- HUD display with color coding\n- All audio feedback implemented\n- Visual animations for placement/removal\n- Per-level reset working\n\n---\n\n## IMPLEMENTATION SUMMARY\n\n### ✅ **FULLY IMPLEMENTED** (9/12 specs)\n1. ✅ Auto-Advance Transitions\n2. ✅ Level Progression\n3. ✅ User Interaction\n4. ✅ Grid Interaction\n5. ✅ UI/Overlay System\n6. ✅ Phase Management\n7. ✅ Scoring System\n8. ✅ Movement Detection\n9. ✅ Canvas Rendering\n10. ✅ Audio Sonification\n11. ✅ Flux Management\n\n### ⚠️ **PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED** (1/12 spec)\n12. ⚠️ Expert Settings / Dev Panel\n\n---\n\n## MISSING FEATURES\n\n### Expert Settings Panel Missing Features:\n1. **Access Methods**:\n   - ❌ Backtick key (`) to open settings\n   - ❌ Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode menu path\n   - ❌ Triple-tap gesture on mobile (top-left corner)\n\n2. **UI Features**:\n   - ❌ Visual indicators showing which values differ from defaults\n   - ❌ Per-section \"Revert\" buttons\n   - ❌ \"Danger Zone\" section for extreme values with warnings\n   - ❌ Live preview of parameter effects (if possible)\n   - ❌ Tooltip documentation for each parameter\n\n3. **Export/Import**:\n   - ❌ \"Export JSON\" button to download current configuration\n   - ❌ \"Import JSON\" file picker to load configuration\n   - ❌ Schema validation for imported JSON\n\n4. **Presets**:\n   - ❌ \"Presets\" dropdown with predefined configurations (Easy, Normal, Hard, Chaos)\n\n5. **Accessibility**:\n   - ❌ Documented parameter explanations (tooltips, help text)\n\n---\n\n## ARCHITECTURAL NOTES\n\nThe implementation demonstrates excellent separation of concerns:\n- **Business logic** in `/src/lib/`: simulation, scoring, movement, flux, phase, level, audio, settings\n- **UI components** in `/src/components/`: Game, GlassHUD, SettingsPanel, CanvasGrid, GridInteraction, ScoreDisplay, FluxDisplay, LevelStats, TransitionOverlay, VictoryScreen, IntroOverlay, UIToggleButton\n- **Custom hooks** in `/src/hooks/`: usePhaseTimer, useTransition\n- **Types** centralized in `/src/types/index.ts`\n- **Comprehensive test coverage** with `.test.ts` and `.test.tsx` files\n\nThe codebase is well-structured, follows React best practices, and has excellent TypeScript typing throughout. All core game mechanics are fully functional and production-ready.\n\n---\n\n## KEY ACHIEVEMENTS\n\n1. **Complete Game Loop**: From intro → planning → countdown → running → finished → transition → next level → victory\n2. **Real-time Scoring**: Dynamic score calculation based on pattern movement and classification\n3. **Visual Excellence**: Age-based neon colors, glow effects, smooth animations, glass UI\n4. **Audio Integration**: Comprehensive sonification with generation sounds, interaction sounds, transition effects\n5. **Resource Management**: Strategic Flux system with phase-based constraints\n6. **Progressive Difficulty**: Multiple scaling modes for replayability\n7. **Accessibility**: Touch-friendly, responsive design, proper touch targets\n8. **Performance**: Canvas rendering, optimized movement detection, minimal re-renders\n9. **Persistence**: High scores, expert settings saved to localStorage\n10. **Developer Experience**: Comprehensive type definitions, test coverage, modular architecture\n\nThe application is **feature-complete for gameplay** with only the expert settings panel's advanced access methods and some UI polish features remaining to be implemented.\n</task_result>","title":"Explore specs directory","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39c2b72d5fferr3GDAlJFz07m0","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771201400103,"end":1771201494857}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771201572689,"sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","part":{"id":"prt_c63d48d2b001aP23iWMjkS1wqB","sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","messageID":"msg_c63d46375001htKZjz90xu8VKt","type":"tool","callID":"call_2085d1a2e2084f648aa6af07","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore source code","prompt":"Exhaustively explore the src directory at /home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/. Map out the entire codebase structure, identify all components, libraries, and hooks. Understand what's currently implemented. Focus on finding gaps between the specs and implementation. Return a comprehensive summary of the current codebase state.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39c2b72c7ffe01fh7fGhpuvDgQ (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nNow let me create a comprehensive summary of the codebase:\n\n---\n\n# Comprehensive Codebase Analysis Summary\n\n## Project Overview\nConway's Game of Life - A gamified version with levels, scoring, progression, audio sonification, and expert settings. Built with React + Vite + TypeScript.\n\n---\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── components/          (13 component files + 12 test files)\n├── hooks/              (2 custom hooks + 1 test file)\n├── lib/                (13 utility files + 13 test files)\n├── styles/             (7 CSS files)\n├── test/               (test setup file)\n├── types/              (1 type definitions file)\n├── App.tsx             (main app entry)\n├── App.test.tsx        (3 tests)\n├── main.tsx            (React DOM entry)\n└── vite-env.d.ts       (Vite type definitions)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 1. Components (13 implemented)\n\n| Component | Purpose | Status | Tests |\n|-----------|---------|--------|-------|\n| **App.tsx** | Main app wrapper | ✅ Implemented | 3 tests |\n| **Game.tsx** | Main game logic orchestration (452 lines) | ✅ Implemented | - |\n| **CanvasGrid.tsx** | Canvas-based grid rendering with animations (218 lines) | ✅ Implemented | 14 tests |\n| **FluxDisplay.tsx** | Flux counter with smooth transitions (74 lines) | ✅ Implemented | - |\n| **GlassHUD.tsx** | Main HUD with all controls (169 lines) | ✅ Implemented | 16 tests |\n| **GridInteraction.tsx** | Grid interaction wrapper (230 lines) | ✅ Implemented | 4 tests |\n| **IntroOverlay.tsx** | Cinematic intro screen (32 lines) | ✅ Implemented | 4 tests |\n| **LevelStats.tsx** | End-of-level statistics display (101 lines) | ✅ Implemented | 15 tests |\n| **ScoreDisplay.tsx** | Score display with animations (130 lines) | ✅ Implemented | 12 tests |\n| **SettingsPanel.tsx** | Expert settings panel (360 lines) | ✅ Implemented | ⚠️ No component tests |\n| **TransitionOverlay.tsx** | Level transition overlay (74 lines) | ✅ Implemented | 6 tests |\n| **VictoryScreen.tsx** | Victory screen for final level (58 lines) | ✅ Implemented | 5 tests |\n| **UIToggleButton.tsx** | UI visibility toggle (44 lines) | ✅ Implemented | 3 tests |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Hooks (2 implemented)\n\n| Hook | Purpose | Status | Tests |\n|------|---------|--------|-------|\n| **usePhaseTimer** | Phase state machine with countdown and timer (135 lines) | ✅ Implemented | - |\n| **useTransition** | Level transition state machine (191 lines) | ✅ Implemented | 1 test |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Libraries (13 implemented)\n\n| Library | Purpose | Status | Tests |\n|---------|---------|--------|-------|\n| **audio.ts** (270 lines) | SoundEngine with Web Audio API | ✅ Implemented | 19 tests |\n| **canvasUtils.ts** (30 lines) | Canvas rendering utilities | ✅ Implemented | - |\n| **flux.ts** (57 lines) | Flux resource management | ✅ Implemented | 22 tests |\n| **interaction.ts** (60 lines) | User input handling | ✅ Implemented | 7 tests |\n| **level.ts** (164 lines) | Level progression & difficulty | ✅ Implemented | 22 tests |\n| **logger.ts** (46 lines) | Logging utility | ✅ Implemented | 11 tests |\n| **movement.ts** (254 lines) | Movement detection & classification | ✅ Implemented | 27 tests |\n| **phase.ts** (166 lines) | Phase state machine | ✅ Implemented | 20 tests |\n| **scoring.ts** (93 lines) | Scoring system | ✅ Implemented | 21 tests |\n| **settings.ts** (126 lines) | Settings management | ✅ Implemented | 25 tests |\n| **simulation.ts** (138 lines) | Game of Life simulation engine | ✅ Implemented | - |\n| **state.ts** (114 lines) | State management utilities | ✅ Implemented | 15 tests |\n| **validation.ts** (56 lines) | Input validation | ✅ Implemented | 27 tests |\n\n---\n\n## 4. CSS Files (7 implemented)\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| **FluxDisplay.css** | Flux counter styles |\n| **GlassHUD.css** | Main HUD glassmorphism styles |\n| **index.css** | Global styles |\n| **IntroOverlay.css** | Intro overlay with glitch effect |\n| **LevelStats.css** | Level statistics styles |\n| **ScoreDisplay.css** | Score display styles |\n| **SettingsPanel.css** | Settings panel styles |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Types (comprehensive)\n\nLocated in `src/types/index.ts` (110 lines):\n\n- ✅ GridType (number[][] - age-based cell storage)\n- ✅ GamePhase enum ('PLANNING' | 'COUNTDOWN' | 'RUNNING' | 'FINISHED')\n- ✅ InteractionMode ('DRAW' | 'ERASE')\n- ✅ TransitionState ('PLAYING' | 'FADING_OUT' | 'INTERSTITIAL' | 'FADING_IN' | 'READY')\n- ✅ CellCluster & TrackedCluster interfaces\n- ✅ RuleSet, SimulationState, FluxState\n- ✅ LevelConfig, ScoringConfig, ScoreState\n- ✅ LevelProgression\n- ✅ DifficultyScalingMode ('TIME_ONLY' | 'RESOURCE_ONLY' | 'MIXED' | 'EXTREME')\n- ✅ LevelGenerationParams, MovementDetectionParams\n- ✅ GridSizingParams, AudioParams, ExpertSettings\n- ✅ TransitionConfig\n\n---\n\n## 6. Test Coverage\n\n**Total Tests: 341 passing**\n\n| Category | Test Files | Tests |\n|----------|------------|-------|\n| Components | 12 files | 94 tests |\n| Hooks | 1 file | 1 test |\n| Lib | 13 files | 246 tests |\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Status vs Specs\n\n### ✅ FULLY IMPLEMENTED (Sprint 1-4)\n\n1. **Project Setup & Build System** (Sprint 1.1)\n   - ✅ React + Vite initialized\n   - ✅ TypeScript strict mode\n   - ✅ ESLint, Prettier configured\n   - ✅ Project structure created\n\n2. **Type Definitions** (Sprint 1.2)\n   - ✅ All core types defined\n   - ✅ All configuration interfaces\n\n3. **Shared Utilities** (Sprint 1.3)\n   - ✅ Validation utilities (validation.ts)\n   - ✅ Logging utility (logger.ts)\n   - ✅ State management (state.ts)\n\n4. **Simulation Engine** (Sprint 1.4)\n   - ✅ Conway's rules with toroidal boundaries\n   - ✅ Age tracking\n   - ✅ Neighbor counting with Moore neighborhood\n   - ✅ Performance optimizations\n   - ✅ Grid resizing (Small/Medium/Large)\n   - ✅ Birth statistics for audio\n\n5. **Phase Management** (Sprint 1.5)\n   - ✅ Phase state machine (PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED)\n   - ✅ Countdown timer (3 seconds)\n   - ✅ Level timer (configurable duration)\n   - ✅ Browser tab handling\n\n6. **Canvas Rendering** (Sprint 1.6)\n   - ✅ DPR scaling\n   - ✅ Responsive cell sizing\n   - ✅ Age-based colors\n   - ✅ Glow effects\n   - ✅ Grid lines toggle\n\n7. **User Interaction** (Sprint 1.7)\n   - ✅ Mouse & touch handling\n   - ✅ Coordinate mapping\n   - ✅ Interaction modes (DRAW/ERASE)\n   - ✅ Cursor states\n\n8. **Flux Management** (Sprint 1.8)\n   - ✅ Flux state tracking\n   - ✅ Placement logic\n   - ✅ Refund mechanic (PLANNING only)\n   - ✅ Flux counter with color coding\n   - ✅ Audio feedback\n\n9. **Grid Interaction** (Sprint 1.9)\n   - ✅ Click-to-place/erase\n   - ✅ Cell preview ghost outline\n   - ✅ Cell animations (birth/death/invalid)\n   - ✅ Minimum cells rule\n   - ✅ Phase-based interaction constraints\n\n10. **Intro Overlay** (Sprint 2.1)\n    - ✅ Cinematic intro with glitch effect\n    - ✅ \"ENTER VOID\" button\n    - ✅ Exit animation (1.2s)\n\n11. **Main UI Controls** (Sprint 2.2)\n    - ✅ Glass HUD container\n    - ✅ Control buttons (STEP, START, RANDOM, CLEAR)\n    - ✅ Interaction mode buttons (DRAW/ERASE)\n    - ✅ Status displays\