ls\n\n20. **Visual Polish** (Sprint 4.2)\n    - ✅ Cell animations (birth fade-in, death shrink)\n    - ✅ Invalid action flash\n    - ✅ Cell preview ghost outline\n    - ✅ Score animation (smooth increment, pulse, milestone)\n    - ✅ Flux counter animation (smooth transitions, color coding)\n    - ✅ Intro glitch effect\n    - ✅ Glass effect polish\n\n21. **Mobile Enhancements** (Sprint 4.3 - Partial)\n    - ✅ touch-action handling\n    - ✅ Minimum touch targets (44×44px)\n    - ⚠️ Touch ripple effect (optional, not implemented)\n    - ⚠️ Mobile expert settings access (triple-tap gesture, not implemented)\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED / NOT IMPLEMENTED (Sprint 5-6)\n\n22. **Expert Settings Panel** (Sprint 5.1 - Partially Complete)\n    - ✅ Settings panel implemented (SettingsPanel.tsx)\n    - ✅ All parameter categories implemented\n    - ✅ Settings persistence to localStorage\n    - ✅ Reset to defaults\n    - ⚠️ Missing: Keyboard shortcut access (backtick)\n    - ⚠️ Missing: Mobile gesture access (triple-tap)\n    - ⚠️ Missing: Export/Import JSON\n    - ⚠️ Missing: Presets (Easy, Normal, Hard, Chaos)\n    - ⚠️ Missing: Danger zone with warnings\n    - ⚠️ Missing: Tooltips/documentation\n    - ⚠️ Missing: SettingsPanel component tests\n\n23. **Presets System** (Sprint 5.2 - Not Implemented)\n    - ❌ Preset configurations (Easy, Normal, Hard, Chaos)\n    - ❌ Preset selection UI\n    - ❌ Custom preset support\n\n24. **Error Handling & Resilience** (Sprint 6.1 - Not Implemented)\n    - ❌ Global error boundary\n    - ❌ Input validation at UI level (only lib-level validation exists)\n    - ❌ Retry mechanisms\n    - ❌ Browser compatibility checks\n\n25. **Accessibility** (Sprint 6.2 - Not Implemented)\n    - ❌ Keyboard navigation (arrow keys for grid, etc.)\n    - ❌ Screen reader support (ARIA labels)\n    - ❌ Reduced motion support\n    - ❌ High contrast mode\n    - ❌ Focus management\n\n26. **Performance Optimization** (Sprint 6.3 - Not Implemented)\n    - ❌ Web Workers for simulation (already fast enough for game grids)\n    - ❌ Object pooling\n    - ❌ Memoization optimizations\n    - ❌ Lazy loading\n\n---\n\n## Key Gaps Between Specs and Implementation\n\n### 1. Missing Accessibility Features (Sprint 6.2)\n- No ARIA labels on UI elements\n- No keyboard navigation for grid (arrow keys)\n- No screen reader announcements for game state\n- No reduced motion media query support\n- No high contrast mode toggle\n\n### 2. Missing Advanced Settings Features (Sprint 5.1-5.2)\n- No keyboard shortcut (`) to open settings\n- No mobile triple-tap gesture for settings\n- No export/import settings JSON\n- No preset system (Easy/Normal/Hard/Chaos)\n- No tooltips explaining parameters\n- No danger zone warnings\n\n### 3. Missing Error Handling (Sprint 6.1)\n- No React error boundary\n- No graceful handling of corrupted localStorage\n- No browser compatibility checks\n- No retry mechanisms for failed operations\n\n### 4. Minor Missing Features\n- Touch ripple effect for mobile\n- SettingsPanel component tests (only lib tests exist)\n\n---\n\n## Technical Highlights\n\n### Architecture Patterns\n- **React Components**: Functional components with hooks\n- **State Management**: useReducer for complex state (phase, transitions)\n- **Custom Hooks**: Encapsulated logic (usePhaseTimer, useTransition)\n- **Utility Libraries**: Pure functions, testable\n- **Type Safety**: Comprehensive TypeScript types\n\n### Performance Optimizations\n- Canvas rendering instead of DOM nodes for grid\n- requestAnimationFrame for 60fps animations\n- React refs to avoid re-renders\n- Precomputed neighbor offset array\n- Double-buffer pattern for simulation\n\n### Code Quality\n- 341 tests passing (94 component + 247 library)\n- Test coverage for core logic\n- Comprehensive type definitions\n- Modular, maintainable structure\n\n---\n\n## Current Game State\n\n**Fully Playable Game:**\n- ✅ 10 levels with progression\n- ✅ 4 difficulty modes\n- ✅ Movement-based scoring\n- ✅ Audio sonification\n- ✅ Smooth animations\n- ✅ Expert settings\n- ✅ Victory screen\n\n**Production Ready:**\n- Core gameplay is complete and polished\n- All major features from Sprints 1-4 implemented\n- Mobile-responsive design\n- Comprehensive test coverage\n\n**Future Enhancements:**\n- Accessibility improvements (Sprint 6.2)\n- Advanced settings features (Sprint 5.1-5.2)\n- Error handling (Sprint 6.1)\n- Performance optimizations (Sprint 6.3)\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThe codebase is in excellent shape with **all core game features implemented**. The game is fully playable with:\n- Complete simulation engine\n- Full level progression (10 levels)\n- Movement detection and scoring\n- Audio sonification\n- Smooth animations and transitions\n- Expert settings panel\n- Victory screen\n\nThe remaining gaps are primarily **quality-of-life features** (accessibility, advanced settings, error handling) rather than core gameplay functionality. The implementation matches the specs for Sprints 1-4 almost completely, with only Sprint 5-6 features being partially or fully unimplemented.\n</task_result>","title":"Explore source code","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39c2b72c7ffe01fh7fGhpuvDgQ","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771201400117,"end":1771201572686}}}}
