{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771201582381,"sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","part":{"id":"prt_c63d75517001nblCPjQzaqWT7t","sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","messageID":"msg_c63d73038001JP5aZ78cnXcHu1","type":"tool","callID":"call_cdc0beb3a3f9423d82959447","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/expert-settings.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/expert-settings.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Expert Settings / Dev Panel\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: Hidden configuration interface for tuning game mechanics, balancing parameters, and debugging. Accessible during development and for advanced users to find optimal parametrization.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Access Methods\n9: ```typescript\n10: interface ExpertSettingsAccess {\n11:   keyboardShortcut: string;      // '`' (backtick) for quick access\n12:   menuPath: string;              // \"Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode\" (if menu system exists)\n13:   gesture: string;               // Mobile: triple-tap top-left corner\n14: }\n15: ```\n16: \n17: ### Configurable Parameters\n18: \n19: #### Movement Detection Parameters\n20: ```typescript\n21: interface MovementDetectionParams {\n22:   centroidHistoryLength: number;       // Generations to track (default: 5, range: 3-10)\n23:   movementThreshold: number;           // Cells to be \"moving\" (default: 0.5, range: 0.1-2.0)\n24:   minClusterSize: number;            // Minimum cells to track (default: 1, range: 1-5)\n25: }\n26: ```\n27: \n28: #### Scoring Parameters\n29: ```typescript\n30: interface ScoringParams {\n31:   moverPointsPerGeneration: number;      // Default: 10, range: 1-100\n32:   oscillatorPointsPerGeneration: number;   // Default: 2, range: 0-20\n33:   scoreMultiplier: number;                // Default: 1.0, range: 0.1-5.0\n34: }\n35: ```\n36: \n37: #### Level Generation Parameters\n38: ```typescript\n39: interface LevelGenerationParams {\n40:   baseTimeSeconds: number;                // Default: 45, range: 10-120\n41:   timeIncrementPerLevel: number;          // Default: 15, range: 0-60\n42:   baseFlux: number;                       // Default: 20, range: 5-50\n43:   difficultyScalingMode: 'TIME_ONLY' | 'RESOURCE_ONLY' | 'MIXED' | 'EXTREME';\n44: }\n45: ```\n46: \n47: #### Grid Sizing Parameters\n48: ```typescript\n49: interface GridSizingParams {\n50:   mobileCellSize: number;                 // Default: 18, range: 14-24\n51:   desktopCellSize: number;                // Default: 20, range: 16-28\n52:   minVisibleCells: number;                // Default: 10, minimum cells visible\n53: }\n54: ```\n55: \n56: ### Settings Persistence\n57: - Save to localStorage under key `gol-expert-settings`\n58: - Load on app startup\n59: - \"Reset to Defaults\" button with confirmation\n60: - Export/Import settings as JSON (for sharing configurations)\n61: \n62: ## UI/UX Requirements\n63: \n64: ### Panel Layout\n65: - **Position**: Modal overlay, centered or right sidebar\n66: - **Sections**: Collapsible groups by category (Movement, Scoring, Levels, Grid)\n67: - **Controls**:\n68:   - Sliders for numeric ranges\n69:   - Number inputs for precise values\n70:   - Dropdowns for mode selection\n71: \n72: ### Real-Time Updates\n73: - Changes apply immediately (no restart required)\n74: - Visual indicator when value differs from default\n75: - \"Revert\" button per section\n76: - Live preview: Show parameter effects in real-time if possible\n77: \n78: ### Danger Zone\n79: - Separate section for \"Break Things\" settings\n80: - Require confirmation for extreme values\n81: - Show warning if settings would make game impossible\n82: \n83: ### Export/Import\n84: - \"Export JSON\" button downloads current config\n85: - \"Import JSON\" file picker loads config\n86: - Validate imported JSON against schema\n87: \n88: ## Edge Cases\n89: \n90: 1. **Invalid Values**: Input validation prevents negative numbers, out-of-range values\n91: 2. **Settings While Running**: Changes to scoring apply immediately; level changes apply on next level\n92: 3. **Reset During Game**: Reset to defaults should warn if game in progress\n93: 4. **Corrupted Storage**: If localStorage has invalid JSON, fall back to defaults\n94: 5. **Mobile Access**: Ensure gesture detection doesn't conflict with game controls\n95: \n96: ## Implementation Notes\n97: \n98: - Use React Context or Zustand for settings state\n99: - Validate all inputs with constraints\n100: - Schema validation using Zod or similar\n101: - Default values should create balanced, playable game\n102: - Consider \"Presets\" dropdown (\"Easy\", \"Normal\", \"Hard\", \"Chaos\")\n103: - Expert settings should be accessible but not intrusive\n104: - Document each parameter with tooltip explaining its effect\n105: \n\n(End of file - total 105 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/expert-settings.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Expert Settings / Dev Panel\n\n## Overview\nHidden configuration interface for tuning game mechanics, balancing parameters, and debugging. Accessible during development and for advanced users to find optimal parametrization.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Access Methods\n```typescript\ninterface ExpertSettingsAccess {\n  keyboardShortcut: string;      // '`' (backtick) for quick access\n  menuPath: string;              // \"Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode\" (if menu system exists)\n  gesture: string;               // Mobile: triple-tap top-left corner\n}\n```\n\n### Configurable Parameters\n\n#### Movement Detection Parameters\n```typescript","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771201582362,"end":1771201582379}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771201582386,"sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","part":{"id":"prt_c63d7551c001v4xyFylc7fcImO","sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","messageID":"msg_c63d73038001JP5aZ78cnXcHu1","type":"tool","callID":"call_1f3c608f1f21446ab00d8913","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: import { useState } from 'react'\n2: import type { ExpertSettings } from '../types'\n3: import '../styles/SettingsPanel.css'\n4: \n5: interface SettingsPanelProps {\n6:   isOpen: boolean\n7:   settings: ExpertSettings\n8:   onClose: () => void\n9:   onUpdateSettings: (settings: ExpertSettings) => void\n10: }\n11: \n12: export function SettingsPanel({ isOpen, settings, onClose, onUpdateSettings }: SettingsPanelProps) {\n13:   const [localSettings, setLocalSettings] = useState(settings)\n14: \n15:   const handleUpdate = (path: string, value: any) => {\n16:     const newSettings = { ...localSettings }\n17:     const keys = path.split('.')\n18:     let target: any = newSettings\n19: \n20:     for (let i = 0; i < keys.length - 1; i++) {\n21:       target = target[keys[i]]\n22:     }\n23: \n24:     target[keys[keys.length - 1]] = value\n25:     setLocalSettings(newSettings)\n26:   }\n27: \n28:   const handleSave = () => {\n29:     onUpdateSettings(localSettings)\n30:     onClose()\n31:   }\n32: \n33:   const handleReset = () => {\n34:     const defaultSettings = {\n35:       movementDetection: {\n36:         centroidHistoryLength: 5,\n37:         movementThreshold: 0.5,\n38:         minClusterSize: 1,\n39:       },\n40:       scoring: {\n41:         moverPointsPerGeneration: 10,\n42:         oscillatorPointsPerGeneration: 2,\n43:         scoreMultiplier: 1.0,\n44:       },\n45:       levelGeneration: {\n46:         baseTimeSeconds: 45,\n47:         timeIncrementPerLevel: 15,\n48:         baseFlux: 20,\n49:         difficultyScalingMode: 'TIME_ONLY' as const,\n50:       },\n51:       gridSizing: {\n52:         mobileCellSize: 18,\n53:         desktopCellSize: 20,\n54:         minVisibleCells: 10,\n55:       },\n56:       audio: {\n57:         enabled: false,\n58:         volume: 0.1,\n59:         waveform: 'sine' as const,\n60:       },\n61:     }\n62:     setLocalSettings(defaultSettings)\n63:   }\n64: \n65:   if (!isOpen) return null\n66: \n67:   return (\n68:     <div className=\"settings-overlay\" onClick={onClose}>\n69:       <div className=\"settings-panel\" onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}>\n70:         <div className=\"settings-header\">\n71:           <h2>Settings</h2>\n72:           <button className=\"close-button\" onClick={onClose}>\n73:             ×\n74:           </button>\n75:         </div>\n76: \n77:         <div className=\"settings-content\">\n78:           <section className=\"settings-section\">\n79:             <h3>Audio</h3>\n80:             <div className=\"settings-row\">\n81:               <label htmlFor=\"audio-enabled\">\n82:                 <input\n83:                   id=\"audio-enabled\"\n84:                   type=\"checkbox\"\n85:                   checked={localSettings.audio.enabled}\n86:                   onChange={(e) => handleUpdate('audio.enabled', e.target.checked)}\n87:                 />\n88:                 Enable Sonification\n89:               </label>\n90:             </div>\n91:             <div className=\"settings-row\">\n92:               <label htmlFor=\"audio-volume\">\n93:                 Volume: {(localSettings.audio.volume * 100).toFixed(0)}%\n94:               </label>\n95:               <input\n96:                 id=\"audio-volume\"\n97:                 type=\"range\"\n98:                 min=\"0\"\n99:                 max=\"0.5\"\n100:                 step=\"0.01\"\n101:                 value={localSettings.audio.volume}\n102:                 onChange={(e) => handleUpdate('audio.volume', parseFloat(e.target.value))}\n103:                 className=\"settings-slider\"\n104:               />\n105:             </div>\n106:             <div className=\"settings-row\">\n107:               <label htmlFor=\"audio-waveform\">Waveform</label>\n108:               <select\n109:                 id=\"audio-waveform\"\n110:                 value={localSettings.audio.waveform}\n111:                 onChange={(e) =>\n112:                   handleUpdate(\n113:                     'audio.waveform',\n114:                     e.target.value as 'sine' | 'triangle' | 'square' | 'sawtooth'\n115:                   )\n116:                 }\n117:                 className=\"settings-select\"\n118:               >\n119:                 <option value=\"sine\">Sine</option>\n120:                 <option value=\"triangle\">Triangle</option>\n121:                 <option value=\"square\">Square</option>\n122:                 <option value=\"sawtooth\">Sawtooth</option>\n123:               </select>\n124:             </div>\n125:           </section>\n126: \n127:           <section className=\"settings-section\">\n128:             <h3>Movement Detection</h3>\n129:             <div className=\"settings-row\">\n130:               <label htmlFor=\"movement-history\">\n131:                 Centroid History Length: {localSettings.movementDetection.centroidHistoryLength}\n132:               </label>\n133:               <input\n134:                 id=\"movement-history\"\n135:                 type=\"range\"\n136:                 min=\"3\"\n137:                 max=\"10\"\n138:                 step=\"1\"\n139:                 value={localSettings.movementDetection.centroidHistoryLength}\n140:                 onChange={(e) =>\n141:                   handleUpdate('movementDetection.centroidHistoryLength', parseInt(e.target.value))\n142:                 }\n143:                 className=\"settings-slider\"\n144:               />\n145:             </div>\n146:             <div className=\"settings-row\">\n147:               <label htmlFor=\"movement-threshold\">\n148:                 Movement Threshold: {localSettings.movementDetection.movementThreshold.toFixed(1)}\n149:               </label>\n150:               <input\n151:                 id=\"movement-threshold\"\n152:                 type=\"range\"\n153:                 min=\"0.1\"\n154:                 max=\"2.0\"\n155:                 step=\"0.1\"\n156:                 value={localSettings.movementDetection.movementThreshold}\n157:                 onChange={(e) =>\n158:                   handleUpdate('movementDetection.movementThreshold', parseFloat(e.target.value))\n159:                 }\n160:                 className=\"settings-slider\"\n161:               />\n162:             </div>\n163:             <div className=\"settings-row\">\n164:               <label htmlFor=\"movement-min-size\">\n165:                 Minimum Cluster Size: {localSettings.movementDetection.minClusterSize}\n166:               </label>\n167:               <input\n168:                 id=\"movement-min-size\"\n169:                 type=\"range\"\n170:                 min=\"1\"\n171:                 max=\"5\"\n172:                 step=\"1\"\n173:                 value={localSettings.movementDetection.minClusterSize}\n174:                 onChange={(e) =>\n175:                   handleUpdate('movementDetection.minClusterSize', parseInt(e.target.value))\n176:                 }\n177:                 className=\"settings-slider\"\n178:               />\n179:             </div>\n180:           </section>\n181: \n182:           <section className=\"settings-section\">\n183:             <h3>Scoring</h3>\n184:             <div className=\"settings-row\">\n185:               <label htmlFor=\"scoring-mover\">\n186:                 Mover Points/Gen: {localSettings.scoring.moverPointsPerGeneration}\n187:               </label>\n188:               <input\n189:                 id=\"scoring-mover\"\n190:                 type=\"range\"\n191:                 min=\"1\"\n192:                 max=\"100\"\n193:                 step=\"1\"\n194:                 value={localSettings.scoring.moverPointsPerGeneration}\n195:                 onChange={(e) =>\n196:                   handleUpdate('scoring.moverPointsPerGeneration', parseInt(e.target.value))\n197:                 }\n198:                 className=\"settings-slider\"\n199:               />\n200:             </div>\n201:             <div className=\"settings-row\">\n202:               <label htmlFor=\"scoring-oscillator\">\n203:                 Oscillator Points/Gen: {localSettings.scoring.oscillatorPointsPerGeneration}\n204:               </label>\n205:               <input\n206:                 id=\"scoring-oscillator\"\n207:                 type=\"range\"\n208:                 min=\"0\"\n209:                 max=\"20\"\n210:                 step=\"1\"\n211:                 value={localSettings.scoring.oscillatorPointsPerGeneration}\n212:                 onChange={(e) =>\n213:                   handleUpdate('scoring.oscillatorPointsPerGeneration', parseInt(e.target.value))\n214:                 }\n215:                 className=\"settings-slider\"\n216:               />\n217:             </div>\n218:             <div className=\"settings-row\">\n219:               <label htmlFor=\"scoring-multiplier\">\n220:                 Score Multiplier: {localSettings.scoring.scoreMultiplier.toFixed(1)}x\n221:               </label>\n222:               <input\n223:                 id=\"scoring-multiplier\"\n224:                 type=\"range\"\n225:                 min=\"0.1\"\n226:                 max=\"5.0\"\n227:                 step=\"0.1\"\n228:                 value={localSettings.scoring.scoreMultiplier}\n229:                 onChange={(e) =>\n230:                   handleUpdate('scoring.scoreMultiplier', parseFloat(e.target.value))\n231:                 }\n232:                 className=\"settings-slider\"\n233:               />\n234:             </div>\n235:           </section>\n236: \n237:           <section className=\"settings-section\">\n238:             <h3>Level Generation</h3>\n239:             <div className=\"settings-row\">\n240:               <label htmlFor=\"level-time\">\n241:                 Base Time (s): {localSettings.levelGeneration.baseTimeSeconds}\n242:               </label>\n243:               <input\n244:                 id=\"level-time\"\n245:                 type=\"range\"\n246:                 min=\"10\"\n247:                 max=\"120\"\n248:                 step=\"5\"\n249:                 value={localSettings.levelGeneration.baseTimeSeconds}\n250:                 onChange={(e) =>\n251:                   handleUpdate('levelGeneration.baseTimeSeconds', parseInt(e.target.value))\n252:                 }\n253:                 className=\"settings-slider\"\n254:               />\n255:             </div>\n256:             <div className=\"settings-row\">\n257:               <label htmlFor=\"level-increment\">\n258:                 Time Increment/Level (s): {localSettings.levelGeneration.timeIncrementPerLevel}\n259:               </label>\n260:               <input\n261:                 id=\"level-increment\"\n262:                 type=\"range\"\n263:                 min=\"0\"\n264:                 max=\"60\"\n265:                 step=\"5\"\n266:                 value={localSettings.levelGeneration.timeIncrementPerLevel}\n267:                 onChange={(e) =>\n268:                   handleUpdate('levelGeneration.timeIncrementPerLevel', parseInt(e.target.value))\n269:                 }\n270:                 className=\"settings-slider\"\n271:               />\n272:             </div>\n273:             <div className=\"settings-row\">\n274:               <label htmlFor=\"level-flux\">\n275:                 Base Flux: {localSettings.levelGeneration.baseFlux}\n276:               </label>\n277:               <input\n278:                 id=\"level-flux\"\n279:                 type=\"range\"\n280:                 min=\"5\"\n281:                 max=\"50\"\n282:                 step=\"5\"\n283:                 value={localSettings.levelGeneration.baseFlux}\n284:                 onChange={(e) => handleUpdate('levelGeneration.baseFlux', parseInt(e.target.value))}\n285:                 className=\"settings-slider\"\n286:               />\n287:             </div>\n288:             <div className=\"settings-row\">\n289:               <label htmlFor=\"level-difficulty\">Difficulty Mode</label>\n290:               <select\n291:                 id=\"level-difficulty\"\n292:                 value={localSettings.levelGeneration.difficultyScalingMode}\n293:                 onChange={(e) =>\n294:                   handleUpdate(\n295:                     'levelGeneration.difficultyScalingMode',\n296:                     e.target.value as 'TIME_ONLY' | 'RESOURCE_ONLY' | 'MIXED' | 'EXTREME'\n297:                   )\n298:                 }\n299:                 className=\"settings-select\"\n300:               >\n301:                 <option value=\"TIME_ONLY\">Time Only</option>\n302:                 <option value=\"RESOURCE_ONLY\">Resource Only</option>\n303:                 <option value=\"MIXED\">Mixed</option>\n304:                 <option value=\"EXTREME\">Extreme</option>\n305:               </select>\n306:             </div>\n307:           </section>\n308: \n309:           <section className=\"settings-section\">\n310:             <h3>Grid Sizing</h3>\n311:             <div className=\"settings-row\">\n312:               <label htmlFor=\"grid-mobile\">\n313:                 Mobile Cell Size (px): {localSettings.gridSizing.mobileCellSize}\n314:               </label>\n315:               <input\n316:                 id=\"grid-mobile\"\n317:                 type=\"range\"\n318:                 min=\"14\"\n319:                 max=\"24\"\n320:                 step=\"2\"\n321:                 value={localSettings.gridSizing.mobileCellSize}\n322:                 onChange={(e) =>\n323:                   handleUpdate('gridSizing.mobileCellSize', parseInt(e.target.value))\n324:                 }\n325:                 className=\"settings-slider\"\n326:               />\n327:             </div>\n328:             <div className=\"settings-row\">\n329:               <label htmlFor=\"grid-desktop\">\n330:                 Desktop Cell Size (px): {localSettings.gridSizing.desktopCellSize}\n331:               </label>\n332:               <input\n333:                 id=\"grid-desktop\"\n334:                 type=\"range\"\n335:                 min=\"16\"\n336:                 max=\"28\"\n337:                 step=\"2\"\n338:                 value={localSettings.gridSizing.desktopCellSize}\n339:                 onChange={(e) =>\n340:                   handleUpdate('gridSizing.desktopCellSize', parseInt(e.target.value))\n341:                 }\n342:                 className=\"settings-slider\"\n343:               />\n344:             </div>\n345:           </section>\n346:         </div>\n347: \n348:         <div className=\"settings-footer\">\n349:           <button className=\"settings-button secondary\" onClick={handleReset}>\n350:             Reset to Defaults\n351:           </button>\n352:           <button className=\"settings-button primary\" onClick={handleSave}>\n353:             Save Settings\n354:           </button>\n355:         </div>\n356:       </div>\n357:     </div>\n358:   )\n359: }\n360: \n\n(End of file - total 360 lines)\n</content>","title":"src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx","metadata":{"preview":"import { useState } from 'react'\nimport type { ExpertSettings } from '../types'\nimport '../styles/SettingsPanel.css'\n\ninterface SettingsPanelProps {\n  isOpen: boolean\n  settings: ExpertSettings\n  onClose: () => void\n  onUpdateSettings: (settings: ExpertSettings) => void\n}\n\nexport function SettingsPanel({ isOpen, settings, onClose, onUpdateSettings }: SettingsPanelProps) {\n  const [localSettings, setLocalSettings] = useState(settings)\n\n  const handleUpdate = (path: string, value: any) => {\n    const newSettings = { ...localSettings }\n    const keys = path.split('.')\n    let target: any = newSettings\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < keys.length - 1; i++) {","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771201582366,"end":1771201582383}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771201582390,"sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","part":{"id":"prt_c63d755200018bg19PpmU9mZhv","sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","messageID":"msg_c63d73038001JP5aZ78cnXcHu1","type":"tool","callID":"call_89040389274147d6aac5ea9c","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: import { useState, useCallback, useEffect, useRef } from 'react'\n2: import { createGrid, GRID_SIZE_PRESETS, type GridSizePreset } from '../lib/simulation'\n3: import {\n4:   type GridType,\n5:   type FluxState,\n6:   type InteractionMode,\n7:   type TrackedCluster,\n8:   type ExpertSettings,\n9:   type LevelProgression,\n10: } from '../types'\n11: import { createInitialFluxState } from '../lib/flux'\n12: import { GridInteraction } from './GridInteraction'\n13: import { usePhaseTimer } from '../hooks/usePhaseTimer'\n14: import { useTransition } from '../hooks/useTransition'\n15: import { stepSimulation, CONWAY_RULES } from '../lib/simulation'\n16: import { findConnectedComponents, trackClusters } from '../lib/movement'\n17: import { createInitialScoreState, updateScore, calculateGenerationScore } from '../lib/scoring'\n18: import { ScoreDisplay } from './ScoreDisplay'\n19: import { GlassHUD } from './GlassHUD'\n20: import { SettingsPanel } from './SettingsPanel'\n21: import { TransitionOverlay } from './TransitionOverlay'\n22: import { VictoryScreen } from './VictoryScreen'\n23: import { UIToggleButton } from './UIToggleButton'\n24: import {\n25:   createInitialExpertSettings,\n26:   saveToLocalStorage,\n27:   loadFromLocalStorage,\n28: } from '../lib/settings'\n29: import {\n30:   generateProgression,\n31:   getCurrentLevelConfig,\n32:   advanceLevel,\n33:   isFinalLevel,\n34:   resetProgression,\n35:   saveHighScore,\n36:   getHighScore,\n37: } from '../lib/level'\n38: import { SoundEngine } from '../lib/audio'\n39: \n40: export function Game() {\n41:   const [gridPreset, setGridPreset] = useState<GridSizePreset>('SMALL')\n42:   const [grid, setGrid] = useState<GridType>(() => createGrid(20, 30))\n43:   const [flux, setFlux] = useState<FluxState>(() => createInitialFluxState(20))\n44:   const [showGridLines, setShowGridLines] = useState(true)\n45:   const [interactionMode, setInteractionMode] = useState<InteractionMode>('DRAW')\n46:   const [generation, setGeneration] = useState(0)\n47:   const [scoreState, setScoreState] = useState(() => createInitialScoreState())\n48:   const [settingsPanelOpen, setSettingsPanelOpen] = useState(false)\n49:   const [expertSettings, setExpertSettings] = useState<ExpertSettings>(() => {\n50:     const saved = loadFromLocalStorage<ExpertSettings>(\n51:       'gol-expert-settings',\n52:       createInitialExpertSettings()\n53:     )\n54:     return saved\n55:   })\n56:   const [levelProgression, setLevelProgression] = useState<LevelProgression>(() =>\n57:     generateProgression(createInitialExpertSettings().levelGeneration)\n58:   )\n59:   const [showVictory, setShowVictory] = useState(false)\n60:   const [isUiVisible, setIsUiVisible] = useState(true)\n61:   const [highScore, setHighScore] = useState(0)\n62:   const [trackedClusters, setTrackedClusters] = useState<TrackedCluster[]>([])\n63:   const [levelStats, setLevelStats] = useState<{\n64:     finalScore: number\n65:     highScore: number\n66:     timeLimitSeconds: number\n67:     timeRemaining: number\n68:     finalGeneration: number\n69:     finalAliveCount: number\n70:     moversCount: number\n71:     oscillatorsCount: number\n72:     staticCount: number\n73:     totalPatternsTracked: number\n74:   } | null>(null)\n75: \n76:   const previousTrackedClustersRef = useRef<TrackedCluster[]>([])\n77:   const previousPhaseRef = useRef<'PLANNING' | 'COUNTDOWN' | 'RUNNING' | 'FINISHED'>('PLANNING')\n78:   const simulationSpeed = 200\n79:   const soundEngineRef = useRef<SoundEngine | null>(null)\n80: \n81:   const {\n82:     enabled: audioEnabled,\n83:     volume: audioVolume,\n84:     waveform: audioWaveform,\n85:   } = expertSettings.audio\n86: \n87:   const handleInteractionSound = useCallback((type: 'draw' | 'erase') => {\n88:     soundEngineRef.current?.playInteractionSound(type)\n89:   }, [])\n90: \n91:   const handleTransitionSound = useCallback((type: 'fade-out' | 'fade-in') => {\n92:     soundEngineRef.current?.playTransitionSound(type)\n93:   }, [])\n94: \n95:   const handleFluxErrorSound = useCallback(() => {\n96:     soundEngineRef.current?.playFluxErrorSound()\n97:   }, [])\n98: \n99:   useEffect(() => {\n100:     if (!soundEngineRef.current) {\n101:       soundEngineRef.current = new SoundEngine()\n102:     }\n103:     soundEngineRef.current.setEnabled(audioEnabled)\n104:     soundEngineRef.current.setVolume(audioVolume)\n105:     soundEngineRef.current.setWaveform(audioWaveform)\n106:   }, [audioEnabled, audioVolume, audioWaveform])\n107: \n108:   const currentLevelConfig = getCurrentLevelConfig(levelProgression)\n109: \n110:   useEffect(() => {\n111:     if (currentLevelConfig) {\n112:       window.requestAnimationFrame(() => {\n113:         setHighScore(getHighScore(currentLevelConfig.levelNumber))\n114:       })\n115:     }\n116:   }, [currentLevelConfig])\n117: \n118:   const movementConfig = expertSettings.movementDetection\n119:   const scoringConfig = expertSettings.scoring\n120: \n121:   const handleTransitionComplete = useCallback(() => {\n122:     soundEngineRef.current?.playLevelStartSound()\n123: \n124:     if (isFinalLevel(levelProgression)) {\n125:       const updatedProgression: LevelProgression = {\n126:         ...levelProgression,\n127:         totalScore: levelProgression.totalScore + scoreState.currentScore,\n128:         currentLevel: levelProgression.currentLevel + 1,\n129:         maxUnlockedLevel: Math.max(\n130:           levelProgression.maxUnlockedLevel,\n131:           levelProgression.currentLevel + 1\n132:         ),\n133:       }\n134:       setLevelProgression(updatedProgression)\n135:       setShowVictory(true)\n136:     } else {\n137:       const newProgression = advanceLevel(levelProgression, scoreState.currentScore)\n138:       const newLevelConfig = getCurrentLevelConfig(newProgression)\n139: \n140:       setLevelProgression(newProgression)\n141:       const { rows, cols } = GRID_SIZE_PRESETS[gridPreset]\n142:       setGrid(createGrid(rows, cols))\n143:       setFlux(createInitialFluxState(newLevelConfig?.initialFlux ?? 20))\n144:       setGeneration(0)\n145:       setScoreState(createInitialScoreState())\n146:       previousTrackedClustersRef.current = []\n147:       setLevelStats(null)\n148:     }\n149:   }, [levelProgression, scoreState.currentScore, gridPreset])\n150: \n151:   const { transitionState, startTransition, resetTransition } = useTransition(\n152:     {\n153:       fadeOutDuration: 2000,\n154:       fadeInDuration: 2000,\n155:       interstitialDuration: 2000,\n156:       autoAdvanceDelay: 2000,\n157:       skipEnabled: true,\n158:     },\n159:     handleTransitionComplete,\n160:     handleTransitionSound\n161:   )\n162: \n163:   const [previousScore, setPreviousScore] = useState(0)\n164: \n165:   const hasCells = useCallback(() => {\n166:     return grid.flat().filter((cell: number) => cell > 0).length > 0\n167:   }, [grid])\n168: \n169:   const { phaseState, startCountdown, startRunning } = usePhaseTimer(hasCells)\n170: \n171:   useEffect(() => {\n172:     if (previousPhaseRef.current === 'COUNTDOWN' && phaseState.current === 'RUNNING') {\n173:       soundEngineRef.current?.playSimulationStartSound()\n174:     }\n175:     previousPhaseRef.current = phaseState.current\n176:   }, [phaseState.current])\n177: \n178:   useEffect(() => {\n179:     if (phaseState.current === 'FINISHED') {\n180:       window.setTimeout(() => {\n181:         if (!showVictory) {\n182:           startTransition()\n183:           soundEngineRef.current?.playLevelCompleteSound()\n184:         }\n185:       }, 2000)\n186:     }\n187:   }, [phaseState, showVictory, startTransition])\n188: \n189:   useEffect(() => {\n190:     if (transitionState === 'READY') {\n191:       window.setTimeout(() => {\n192:         resetTransition()\n193:       }, 100)\n194:     }\n195:   }, [transitionState, resetTransition])\n196: \n197:   useEffect(() => {\n198:     if (phaseState.current === 'FINISHED' && currentLevelConfig && scoreState.currentScore > 0) {\n199:       saveHighScore(currentLevelConfig.levelNumber, scoreState.currentScore)\n200:       window.requestAnimationFrame(() => {\n201:         setHighScore(getHighScore(currentLevelConfig.levelNumber))\n202:       })\n203: \n204:       const staticCount = trackedClusters.filter((c) => c.classification === 'STATIC').length\n205:       const movers = trackedClusters.filter((c) => c.classification === 'MOVER').length\n206:       const oscillators = trackedClusters.filter((c) => c.classification === 'OSCILLATOR').length\n207:       const aliveCount = grid.flat().filter((cell: number) => cell > 0).length\n208: \n209:       setLevelStats({\n210:         finalScore: scoreState.currentScore,\n211:         highScore: getHighScore(currentLevelConfig.levelNumber),\n212:         timeLimitSeconds: currentLevelConfig.timeLimitSeconds,\n213:         timeRemaining: phaseState.timerRemaining,\n214:         finalGeneration: generation,\n215:         finalAliveCount: aliveCount,\n216:         moversCount: movers,\n217:         oscillatorsCount: oscillators,\n218:         staticCount: staticCount,\n219:         totalPatternsTracked: scoreState.totalPatternsTracked,\n220:       })\n221:     }\n222:   }, [phaseState, currentLevelConfig, scoreState, generation, grid, trackedClusters])\n223: \n224:   const handleSimulationStep = useCallback(() => {\n225:     const currentState = {\n226:       grid,\n227:       generation,\n228:       running: true,\n229:       speed: simulationSpeed,\n230:       selectedRule: CONWAY_RULES,\n231:     }\n232: \n233:     const result = stepSimulation(currentState)\n234: \n235:     if (result.bornCount > 0) {\n236:       const totalRows = grid.length\n237:       soundEngineRef.current?.playGenerationSound(result.bornCount, result.averageRow, totalRows)\n238:     }\n239: \n240:     const currentClusters = findConnectedComponents(result.newGrid, result.newGeneration)\n241:     const tracked = trackClusters(currentClusters, trackedClusters, movementConfig)\n242: \n243:     const generationScore = calculateGenerationScore(tracked, scoringConfig)\n244:     const newScoreState = updateScore(scoreState, generationScore)\n245: \n246:     setPreviousScore(scoreState.currentScore)\n247:     previousTrackedClustersRef.current = tracked\n248:     setTrackedClusters(tracked)\n249:     setScoreState(newScoreState)\n250:     setGrid(result.newGrid)\n251:     setGeneration(result.newGeneration)\n252:   }, [\n253:     grid,\n254:     generation,\n255:     simulationSpeed,\n256:     scoreState,\n257:     movementConfig,\n258:     scoringConfig,\n259:     trackedClusters,\n260:   ])\n261: \n262:   useEffect(() => {\n263:     let interval: number | undefined\n264: \n265:     if (phaseState.current === 'RUNNING') {\n266:       interval = window.setInterval(() => {\n267:         handleSimulationStep()\n268:       }, simulationSpeed)\n269:     }\n270: \n271:     return () => {\n272:       if (interval) {\n273:         window.clearInterval(interval)\n274:       }\n275:     }\n276:   }, [phaseState, simulationSpeed, handleSimulationStep, trackedClusters])\n277: \n278:   const handleStart = useCallback(() => {\n279:     if (phaseState.current === 'PLANNING' && hasCells() && currentLevelConfig) {\n280:       startCountdown()\n281:       startRunning(currentLevelConfig.timeLimitSeconds)\n282:     }\n283:   }, [phaseState, startCountdown, hasCells, currentLevelConfig, startRunning])\n284: \n285:   const handleGridChange = useCallback((newGrid: GridType) => {\n286:     setGrid(newGrid)\n287:     setGeneration(0)\n288:   }, [])\n289: \n290:   const handleFluxChange = useCallback((newFlux: FluxState) => {\n291:     setFlux(newFlux)\n292:   }, [])\n293: \n294:   const handleClear = useCallback(() => {\n295:     const { rows, cols } = GRID_SIZE_PRESETS[gridPreset]\n296:     setGrid(createGrid(rows, cols))\n297:     setFlux(createInitialFluxState(20))\n298:     setGeneration(0)\n299:     setScoreState(createInitialScoreState())\n300:     setTrackedClusters([])\n301:     setLevelStats(null)\n302:   }, [gridPreset])\n303: \n304:   const handleRandom = useCallback(() => {\n305:     const { rows, cols } = GRID_SIZE_PRESETS[gridPreset]\n306:     const newGrid = createGrid(rows, cols)\n307:     const density = 0.15\n308: \n309:     for (let row = 0; row < rows; row++) {\n310:       for (let col = 0; col < cols; col++) {\n311:         if (Math.random() < density) {\n312:           newGrid[row][col] = 1\n313:         }\n314:       }\n315:     }\n316: \n317:     setGrid(newGrid)\n318:     setFlux(createInitialFluxState(20))\n319:     setGeneration(0)\n320:     setScoreState(createInitialScoreState())\n321:     setTrackedClusters([])\n322:     setLevelStats(null)\n323:   }, [gridPreset])\n324: \n325:   const aliveCount = grid.flat().filter((cell: number) => cell > 0).length\n326: \n327:   const handleToggleSettings = useCallback(() => {\n328:     setSettingsPanelOpen((prev) => !prev)\n329:   }, [])\n330: \n331:   const handleUpdateSettings = useCallback((newSettings: ExpertSettings) => {\n332:     setExpertSettings(newSettings)\n333:     saveToLocalStorage('gol-expert-settings', newSettings)\n334:   }, [])\n335: \n336:   const handleStep = useCallback(() => {\n337:     if (phaseState.current !== 'PLANNING') return\n338: \n339:     const currentState = {\n340:       grid,\n341:       generation,\n342:       running: false,\n343:       speed: 100,\n344:       selectedRule: CONWAY_RULES,\n345:     }\n346: \n347:     const result = stepSimulation(currentState)\n348:     setGrid(result.newGrid)\n349:     setGeneration(result.newGeneration)\n350:   }, [phaseState, grid, generation])\n351: \n352:   const canInteract = phaseState.current === 'PLANNING'\n353: \n354:   const movers = trackedClusters.filter((c) => c.classification === 'MOVER').length\n355:   const oscillators = trackedClusters.filter((c) => c.classification === 'OSCILLATOR').length\n356:   const rate =\n357:     scoringConfig.moverPointsPerGeneration * movers +\n358:     scoringConfig.oscillatorPointsPerGeneration * oscillators\n359: \n360:   return (\n361:     <div style={{ padding: '20px', backgroundColor: '#0a0a0f', minHeight: '100vh', color: '#fff' }}>\n362:       <UIToggleButton isVisible={isUiVisible} onToggle={() => setIsUiVisible(!isUiVisible)} />\n363: \n364:       <ScoreDisplay\n365:         score={scoreState.currentScore}\n366:         previousScore={previousScore}\n367:         showPatternBreakdown={true}\n368:         movers={movers}\n369:         oscillators={oscillators}\n370:         rate={rate}\n371:         highScore={highScore}\n372:       />\n373: \n374:       <SettingsPanel\n375:         isOpen={settingsPanelOpen}\n376:         settings={expertSettings}\n377:         onClose={() => setSettingsPanelOpen(false)}\n378:         onUpdateSettings={handleUpdateSettings}\n379:       />\n380: \n381:       <h1 style={{ textAlign: 'center', marginBottom: '20px', color: '#61dafb' }}>\n382:         Level {levelProgression.currentLevel} - Conway's Game of Life\n383:       </h1>\n384: \n385:       <TransitionOverlay\n386:         transitionState={transitionState}\n387:         currentLevel={levelProgression.currentLevel}\n388:         showStats={!!levelStats}\n389:         stats={levelStats ?? undefined}\n390:       />\n391: \n392:       {showVictory && (\n393:         <VictoryScreen\n394:           totalScore={levelProgression.totalScore}\n395:           finalLevelStats={levelStats ?? undefined}\n396:           onPlayAgain={() => {\n397:             const reset = resetProgression()\n398:             setLevelProgression(reset)\n399:             setShowVictory(false)\n400:             const { rows, cols } = GRID_SIZE_PRESETS[gridPreset]\n401:             setGrid(createGrid(rows, cols))\n402:             setFlux(createInitialFluxState(reset.levels[0]?.initialFlux ?? 20))\n403:             setGeneration(0)\n404:             setScoreState(createInitialScoreState())\n405:             previousTrackedClustersRef.current = []\n406:             setLevelStats(null)\n407:           }}\n408:         />\n409:       )}\n410: \n411:       {isUiVisible && (\n412:         <GlassHUD\n413:           phase={phaseState.current}\n414:           aliveCount={aliveCount}\n415:           flux={flux.current}\n416:           fluxMax={flux.initial}\n417:           interactionMode={interactionMode}\n418:           gridPreset={gridPreset}\n419:           showGridLines={showGridLines}\n420:           generation={generation}\n421:           countdownValue={phaseState.countdownValue}\n422:           timerRemaining={phaseState.timerRemaining}\n423:           canStart={aliveCount > 0}\n424:           canInteract={canInteract}\n425:           onStart={handleStart}\n426:           onStep={handleStep}\n427:           onClear={handleClear}\n428:           onRandom={handleRandom}\n429:           onToggleGrid={() => setShowGridLines(!showGridLines)}\n430:           onSetMode={setInteractionMode}\n431:           onSetGridPreset={setGridPreset}\n432:           onToggleSettings={handleToggleSettings}\n433:         />\n434:       )}\n435: \n436:       <div style={{ display: 'flex', justifyContent: 'center' }}>\n437:         <GridInteraction\n438:           grid={grid}\n439:           flux={flux}\n440:           phase={phaseState.current}\n441:           showGridLines={showGridLines}\n442:           onGridChange={handleGridChange}\n443:           onFluxChange={handleFluxChange}\n444:           interactionMode={interactionMode}\n445:           onInteractionSound={handleInteractionSound}\n446:           onFluxErrorSound={handleFluxErrorSound}\n447:         />\n448:       </div>\n449:     </div>\n450:   )\n451: }\n452: \n\n(End of file - total 452 lines)\n</content>","title":"src/components/Game.tsx","metadata":{"preview":"import { useState, useCallback, useEffect, useRef } from 'react'\nimport { createGrid, GRID_SIZE_PRESETS, type GridSizePreset } from '../lib/simulation'\nimport {\n  type GridType,\n  type FluxState,\n  type InteractionMode,\n  type TrackedCluster,\n  type ExpertSettings,\n  type LevelProgression,\n} from '../types'\nimport { createInitialFluxState } from '../lib/flux'\nimport { GridInteraction } from './GridInteraction'\nimport { usePhaseTimer } from '../hooks/usePhaseTimer'\nimport { useTransition } from '../hooks/useTransition'\nimport { stepSimulation, CONWAY_RULES } from '../lib/simulation'\nimport { findConnectedComponents, trackClusters } from '../lib/movement'\nimport { createInitialScoreState, updateScore, calculateGenerationScore } from '../lib/scoring'\nimport { ScoreDisplay } from './ScoreDisplay'\nimport { GlassHUD } from './GlassHUD'\nimport { SettingsPanel } from './SettingsPanel'","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771201582370,"end":1771201582388}}}}
