{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771201657509,"sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","part":{"id":"prt_c63d77abc001A7B7oXNsDe2tYl","sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","messageID":"msg_c63d7560b001XOTfI8EgozdMdB","type":"tool","callID":"call_cac7a4d11aa34845b9039476","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Search mobile gestures","prompt":"Search the codebase for any existing mobile gesture implementations, particularly triple-tap detection. Look for touch event handlers (touchstart, touchend, touchmove), gesture detection code, or any mobile-specific interaction patterns. Also check for any mentions of gestures, triple-tap, or mobile shortcuts.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39c288539ffeDX8OnDX2RKdYwR (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n## Summary: Mobile Gesture Implementations Search Results\n\nBased on my thorough search of the codebase, here are my findings:\n\n### Touch Event Handling - IMPLEMENTED\n\n**Location:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/interaction.ts`\n- Function `getCellFromEvent` (lines 6-38) handles both `MouseEvent` and `TouchEvent`\n- Touch detection logic (lines 22-26):\n  ```typescript\n  if (event instanceof MouseEvent) {\n    clientX = event.clientX\n    clientY = event.clientY\n  } else {\n    const touch = event.touches[0] || event.changedTouches[0]\n    clientX = touch.clientX\n    clientY = touch.clientY\n  }\n  ```\n\n**Location:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GridInteraction.tsx`\n- `handleCanvasClick` (lines 126-138) accepts `React.MouseEvent | React.TouchEvent`\n- `handleCanvasMove` (lines 140-156) accepts both mouse and touch events\n\n**Location:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx`\n- Line 211: `touch-action: none` style property on canvas element\n- Touch event types defined in props (lines 26-32)\n\n### Triple-Tap Detection - NOT IMPLEMENTED\n\n**Status:** This feature is only planned in specifications, not yet implemented.\n\n**Evidence:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/expert-settings.md` (line 13): Mentions `gesture: string; // Mobile: triple-tap top-left corner`\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (lines 1007-1009): Lists \"Implement mobile expert settings access - Triple-tap top-left corner gesture\" as incomplete\n\n### Other Gestures - NOT FOUND\n\nNo implementations of:\n- Swipe detection\n- Pinch/zoom gestures  \n- Multi-touch gestures\n- Double-click/tap detection\n- Gesture detection libraries\n\n### Existing Mobile Support\n\n**Implemented mobile features:**\n1. Touch-action: none to prevent scroll/zoom during interaction\n2. Responsive cell sizing (18px mobile vs 20px desktop)\n3. Minimum touch targets (44x44px buttons in GlassHUD)\n4. Touch coordinate conversion with device pixel ratio support\n5. Test coverage for touch events in `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/interaction.test.ts` (lines 20-41)\n\n### Conclusion\n\nThe codebase has basic touch event handling for canvas interactions (placing/removing cells), but **no gesture detection** exists, including no triple-tap implementation. Triple-tap is mentioned only as a planned feature in the specification files and implementation plan, but has not been coded yet.\n</task_result>","title":"Search mobile gestures","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39c288539ffeDX8OnDX2RKdYwR","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771201592003,"end":1771201657508}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771201666694,"sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","part":{"id":"prt_c63d77ade001zHvqb4XnEuoU4p","sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","messageID":"msg_c63d7560b001XOTfI8EgozdMdB","type":"tool","callID":"call_bd1895ade43049eb8248ade1","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Search presets implementation","prompt":"Search the codebase for any existing preset system for expert settings. Look for preset configurations (Easy, Normal, Hard, Chaos), preset dropdowns, preset selection UI, or any code that loads/saves preset configurations. Also check for preset-related types, constants, or state management.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39c288514ffetNz6jB59OWDvOa (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my search of the codebase, here's what I found regarding preset systems for expert settings:\n\n## Summary: No Preset System Exists for Expert Settings\n\nThe codebase does **NOT** have an existing preset system for expert settings (Easy, Normal, Hard, Chaos). However, there are some related preset implementations:\n\n---\n\n## Existing Preset-Related Code\n\n### 1. **Grid Size Presets** (Implemented)\n**Location:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/simulation.ts` (lines 123-133)\n\n```typescript\nexport type GridSizePreset = 'SMALL' | 'MEDIUM' | 'LARGE'\n\nexport const GRID_SIZE_PRESETS: Record<GridSizePreset, { rows: number; cols: number }> = {\n  SMALL: { rows: 20, cols: 30 },\n  MEDIUM: { rows: 40, cols: 50 },\n  LARGE: { rows: 60, cols: 80 },\n}\n```\n\n**Usage:** These are selectable buttons in the GlassHUD component:\n- File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.tsx` (lines 101-123)\n- File: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx` (lines 41, 141, 295, 305, 400)\n\n### 2. **Difficulty Scaling Mode** (Partial Preset)\n**Location:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/types/index.ts` (line 68)\n\n```typescript\nexport type DifficultyScalingMode = 'TIME_ONLY' | 'RESOURCE_ONLY' | 'MIXED' | 'EXTREME'\n```\n\n**Usage:** This is a dropdown in the SettingsPanel that controls level generation scaling, but it's only a single parameter, not a full preset system.\n\n---\n\n## Expert Settings System (Implemented)\n\n**Location:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`\n\nThe SettingsPanel provides individual slider controls for all expert parameters, but **no preset dropdown**:\n\n- Movement Detection: centroidHistoryLength, movementThreshold, minClusterSize\n- Scoring: moverPointsPerGeneration, oscillatorPointsPerGeneration, scoreMultiplier\n- Level Generation: baseTimeSeconds, timeIncrementPerLevel, baseFlux, difficultyScalingMode\n- Grid Sizing: mobileCellSize, desktopCellSize\n- Audio: enabled, volume, waveform\n\n**Persistence:** Settings are saved to localStorage under key `'gol-expert-settings'` (lines 50-55 in Game.tsx)\n\n---\n\n## What's Missing (Not Implemented)\n\nAccording to the spec and implementation plan:\n\n**Spec Reference:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/expert-settings.md` (line 102)\n- Mentions: \"Consider 'Presets' dropdown ('Easy', 'Normal', 'Hard', 'Chaos')\"\n\n**Implementation Plan:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (lines 1078-1092)\n- Sprint 5.2: \"Presets System (LOW - Convenience)\" is marked as NOT IMPLEMENTED\n- Planned features:\n  - Preset configurations: Easy, Normal, Hard, Chaos\n  - Preset selection UI (dropdown)\n  - Custom preset support (save current settings as preset)\n\n---\n\n## Key Files for Preset Implementation\n\nIf you were to implement the preset system, these are the relevant files:\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/settings.ts` | Settings creation and validation functions |\n| `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/types/index.ts` | ExpertSettings type definition |\n| `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx` | Where the preset dropdown should be added |\n| `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx` | Settings state management |\n| `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/state.ts` | localStorage persistence utilities |\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion\n\n**No preset system for expert settings exists.** You would need to implement:\n1. Preset type definitions (`ExpertSettingsPreset: 'EASY' | 'NORMAL' | 'HARD' | 'CHAOS'`)\n2. Preset configurations object with full ExpertSettings for each preset\n3. Preset selection dropdown in SettingsPanel\n4. Functions to load preset values into the current settings\n\nThe existing grid size preset system (Small/Medium/Large) could serve as a reference for implementation patterns.\n</task_result>","title":"Search presets implementation","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39c288514ffetNz6jB59OWDvOa","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771201592041,"end":1771201666693}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771201667933,"sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","part":{"id":"prt_c63d77acb001E1bs0eG9U83gRd","sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","messageID":"msg_c63d7560b001XOTfI8EgozdMdB","type":"tool","callID":"call_a926a764521f4cad86615810","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Search export/import functionality","prompt":"Search the codebase for any existing export/import JSON functionality for settings. Look for file download/upload, JSON import/export, blob creation, file reader implementations, or any settings export/import code. Also check if there are any buttons or UI elements for export/import.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39c288526ffe4v71cyhSf34uqi (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my comprehensive search of the codebase, here are my findings regarding export/import JSON functionality for settings:\n\n## Summary\n\n**No existing export/import JSON functionality is currently implemented.**\n\n## What Exists\n\n### 1. **Settings Persistence via localStorage**\n- Location: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/state.ts` (lines 79-102)\n- Functions: `saveToLocalStorage()` and `loadFromLocalStorage()`\n- Settings are stored under the key: `'gol-expert-settings'`\n- This is used in `Game.tsx` (lines 50-55, 333) to persist settings between sessions\n\n### 2. **Settings Panel UI**\n- Location: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`\n- **Only two buttons exist in the footer:**\n  - \"Reset to Defaults\" (line 349-351)\n  - \"Save Settings\" (line 352-354)\n- No export/import buttons present\n\n### 3. **Specification Requirement**\n- Location: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/expert-settings.md`\n- Lines 60 and 83-87 specify that export/import JSON is a **planned feature**:\n  ```markdown\n  - Export/Import settings as JSON (for sharing configurations)\n  \n  ### Export/Import\n  - \"Export JSON\" button downloads current config\n  - \"Import JSON\" file picker loads config\n  - Validate imported JSON against schema\n  ```\n\n## What Does NOT Exist\n\n### 1. **No File Download Functionality**\n- No Blob creation found\n- No `URL.createObjectURL()` usage\n- No `<a>` tag download implementation\n- No data URL generation\n\n### 2. **No File Upload Functionality**\n- No `<input type=\"file\">` elements found\n- No FileReader implementation\n- No file picker dialogs\n- No JSON parsing from uploaded files\n\n### 3. **No Export/Import UI Elements**\n- No \"Export JSON\" button\n- No \"Import JSON\" button\n- No file input controls in any component\n- No export/import handlers in any React components\n\n### 4. **No Related Code Patterns**\n- No `exportSettings()` or `importSettings()` functions\n- No `handleExport()` or `handleImport()` event handlers\n- No JSON file validation logic\n- No schema validation for imported configurations (other than the existing `validateExpertSettings()` function)\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe export/import JSON functionality is **specified as a requirement** in the documentation but has **not been implemented yet**. The current implementation only supports:\n- Manual settings adjustment through the SettingsPanel UI\n- Automatic persistence to localStorage\n- Reset to defaults functionality\n\nTo implement this feature, you would need to add:\n1. \"Export JSON\" and \"Import JSON\" buttons in SettingsPanel\n2. File download logic using Blob and URL.createObjectURL\n3. File upload handling with FileReader\n4. JSON validation for imported settings\n5. Integration with the existing validation function (`validateExpertSettings()`)\n</task_result>","title":"Search export/import functionality","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39c288526ffe4v71cyhSf34uqi","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771201592022,"end":1771201667931}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771201672741,"sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","part":{"id":"prt_c63d77ab5001dW09aJr80IgVPf","sessionID":"ses_39c2bb03bffeUY5Iet1Cj0VNDG","messageID":"msg_c63d7560b001XOTfI8EgozdMdB","type":"tool","callID":"call_37cdbf94ea7849edb1373cbe","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Search keyboard shortcuts","prompt":"Search the entire codebase for any existing keyboard shortcut implementations, particularly for the backtick (`) key. Check if there are any keydown event listeners, keyboard event handlers, or keyboard-related hooks. Also check if there's any mention of backtick, key codes, or keyboard shortcuts in comments or documentation.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39c288545ffe7gbUJ7H87JQhck (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my comprehensive search of the codebase, here are my findings regarding keyboard shortcut implementations:\n\n## Existing Keyboard Implementations\n\n### 1. Active Keyboard Event Listener\n**Location:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/hooks/useTransition.ts`\n\n- **Lines 90-96:** Keydown event handler that listens for transition skip functionality\n- **Lines 170, 173:** Adds and removes keydown event listeners on the window object\n- **Supported Keys:**\n  - `'Space'` - Skip transition\n  - `'Escape'` - Skip transition\n\n**Code Pattern Used:**\n```typescript\nconst handleKeyDown = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {\n  if (config.skipEnabled && (e.code === 'Space' || e.code === 'Escape')) {\n    skipTransition()\n  }\n}\n\nwindow.addEventListener('keydown', handleKeyDown)\n```\n\n### 2. Keyboard Event Tests\n**Location:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/hooks/useTransition.test.ts`\n\n- Tests for Space and Escape key handlers (lines 25, 34, 43, 52, 76, 87)\n- Uses `new KeyboardEvent('keydown', { code: 'Space' })` pattern\n\n### 3. UI Keyboard Hints\n**Location:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/TransitionOverlay.tsx`\n\n- **Lines 65, 69:** Displays \"Press Space or ESC to skip\" hint to users\n\n## Planned/Documented Keyboard Shortcuts (Not Implemented)\n\n### 1. Backtick Key for Expert Settings\n**Documentation:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/expert-settings.md` (line 11): \"keyboardShortcut: string; // '`' (backtick) for quick access\"\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (line 1022): \"Access via keyboard shortcut (`), Settings menu, or mobile gesture\"\n\n**Status:** Planned but not implemented\n\n### 2. 'G' Key for Grid Toggle\n**Documentation:**\n- `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/canvas-rendering.md` (line 32): \"Visibility: Toggleable (keyboard shortcut: 'G' key)\"\n\n**Status:** Planned but not implemented\n\n## Key Findings Summary\n\n1. **Only ONE active keyboard implementation exists** - the transition skip functionality in `useTransition.ts`\n2. **No dedicated keyboard hooks or utilities** - no `useKeyboard`, `useKey`, or similar patterns found\n3. **No global keyboard event handler at app level** - `App.tsx` and `main.tsx` have no keyboard listeners\n4. **Backtick key is NOT implemented** - only documented as a planned feature for expert settings access\n5. **Keyboard code pattern:** The codebase uses `e.code` property (e.g., `'Space'`, `'Escape'`) for key detection\n\n## Keyboard Code Standards Used\n\nThe existing implementation follows the pattern:\n- Uses `KeyboardEvent` interface\n- Checks `e.code` property (not `e.key` or `e.keyCode`)\n- Registers listeners on the global `window` object\n- Properly cleans up listeners on unmount\n\n## Recommendations\n\nIf you need to implement keyboard shortcuts (including backtick), you can follow the existing pattern from `useTransition.ts`:\n1. Create a keydown event handler\n2. Check `e.code` against the desired key (for backtick, use `'Backquote'`)\n3. Add listener to `window`\n4. Clean up on unmount\n</task_result>","title":"Search keyboard shortcuts","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39c288545ffe7gbUJ7H87JQhck","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771201591992,"end":1771201672739}}}}
